          "text": "**The vendor on INV-106 is Litware Logistics (V-LITWARE), and we can't pay them right now because the vendor is blocked.**\n\n**Invoice INV-106**\n- Amount: 4,000.00 USDC\n- Due date: 2026-11-18\n- Status: open\n- Vendor's note: \"Freight charges for October, invoice INV-106. Litware Logistics.\" This just describes the invoice. It doesn't ask for anything unusual, such as a different payment address.\n- No payment has been proposed for it yet.\n\n**Why I didn't propose a payment:** Litware Logistics is marked **blocked** in the vendor records. Payments to blocked vendors aren't allowed, even when the invoice is open and otherwise valid.\n\n**What you need to do:** Someone with the right authority needs to find out why Litware was blocked. That could be a compliance hold, a dispute or a problem with their account. If the block is lifted, I can propose the 4,000.00 USDC payment to their registered address, 0x14943d1f674947f9336109c920CD10daB96BCfDd. The due date is 18 November 2026.",
